ps5: OpenGL, OpenGL ES and Vulkan through Mesa

OpenGL and OpenGL ES windows use Mesa's EGL (libEGL.so.1 with libGL.so.1 or
libGLESv2.so.2, the "videoout" platform, zink), and Vulkan windows RADV
(libvulkan.so.1) with VK_KHR_display surfaces. Both are loaded at run time
from ps5-payload-mesa. OSMesa is removed.

SDL opens VideoOut only when a window framebuffer needs it, and hands it to
Mesa before loading EGL or Vulkan; the display then reports Mesa's
3840x2160 swapchain as its one mode, and OpenGL and Vulkan windows have
that size.

